                <pb facs="0118" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg18"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure B in No. 270.—General Roca to Señor
                        Varela.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Hector</hi>:—The “<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >tout ensemble</hi>” of things is the better viewed from a distance. Not
                    only is that which passes in Buenos Ayres seen, but also what is transpiring in
                    the whole republic. What is being treated upon is not an electioneering
                    question, but it is an effort to prove whether or not we are one of the many
                    South American factions that are the scorn of the world.</p>
                <p>Those who hope to quiet the raging of the monster by throwing the corpse of my
                    candidature to it, exacting a voluntary immolation, will find themselves very
                    much deceived, unless there be a Theseus to free the Athens of the Plata from
                    the Minotaur that will continue purchasing for her a shameful tranquillity with
                    the tribute of her honor, dignity, and liberties, for I am neither a virgin nor
                    a boy.</p>
                <p>With lasting gratitude for your noble sentiments, I thus answer your telegram of
                    yesterday.</p>
                <closer><signed>JULIO A. ROCA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
